findings.remediation:
Sanitize the reflected value before outputting it to the browser, e.g.:

```php
// Replace the unsanitized echo with:
echo htmlspecialchars($_GET['password'], ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE, 'UTF-8');
```

This converts any HTML‑special characters (including `<`, `>`, `&`, `"`) into safe entities, preventing the injected script from being executed. Ensure all user‑controlled data that is echoed back is processed with `htmlspecialchars()` (or a equivalent escaping function).

Sanitize the POST value before appending it to the page buffer and use `htmlspecialchars()` to escape any HTML/JS characters.  

```php
if (isset($_POST['include'])) {
    $page['body'] .= htmlspecialchars($_POST['include'], ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
}
```  

This prevents untrusted input from being injected into the rendered HTML.

